# Tales from Two Textbooks: A Comparison of the Civil Rights Movement in Two Secondary History Textbooks.

**Authors:** Epstein, Terrie L.

## Abstract
Contends that differences in historical interpretations presented in textbooks have implications for citizenship education. Compares the treatment of the civil rights movement in two secondary level U.S. history textbooks. Concludes that selection committees should examine historical interpretation as well the amount of information about marginalized groups. (CFR)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ487227

